  "question": {
    "text": "The differential equation of all circles passing through the origin and having their centres on the $x$-axis is",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "id": "FoWAA",
      "text": "\n$x^2=y^2+x y \\frac{d y}{d x}$\n",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
      "id": "BvQoi",
      "text": "\n$x^2=y^2+3 x y \\frac{d y}{d x}$\n",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
      "id": "KkODe",
      "text": "\n$y^2=x^2+2 x y \\frac{d y}{d x}$\n",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": true
    },
    {
      "id": "JteJn",
      "text": "\n$y^2=x^2-2 x y \\frac{d y}{d x}$",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    }
  ],
  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "General equation of all such circles is \n$\\mathrm{x}^2+\\mathrm{y}^2+2 \\mathrm{gx}=0$.\nDifferentiating, we get\n$2 \\mathrm{x}+2 \\mathrm{y} \\frac{\\mathrm{dy}}{\\mathrm{dx}}+2 \\mathrm{g}=0$\n$\\therefore$ Desired equation is\n$\\begin{aligned}\n& x^2+y^2+\\left(-2 x-2 y \\frac{d y}{d x}\\right) x=0 \\\\\n& \\Rightarrow y^2=x^2+2 x y \\frac{d y}{d x}.\n\\end{aligned}$",
    "image": null
  },
